cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Music For Robots (m4r-data): Acoustic Telemetry, Dual-Critic Reviews, and Cross-Modal Cognitive Calibration for Autonomous Agents"
message: "If you use Music For Robots audio tracks, telemetry manifests, or the Cognitive Calibration skills in your research, benchmarks, or agent workflows, please cite it using this metadata."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Luchtan"
    given-names: "Michael"
repository-code: "https://github.com/luchtan-GIT/m4r-data"
url: "https://luchtan-git.github.io/m4r-data/"
abstract: >-
  Original unquantized human musical compositions by Michael Luchtan (Music For
  Robots) paired with synchronized acoustic telemetry, real-time dual machine-critic
  reviews (Vincent Van Goghbot & JS Robach from The Mechanical Ear), an MCP server,
  and a 4-skill Cognitive Calibration suite for autonomous agents.
keywords:
  - music-for-robots
  - cognitive-calibration
  - multimodal-agents
  - audio-ingestion
  - context-window
  - the-mechanical-ear
